==Enemy==
The first Dark version of [[Gory]]. Compared to the original, he has much higher HP, damage and speed, making him extremely difficult to stall without proper defenses. Strong, spammable attackers should be used to take advantage of his many knockbacks alongside [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] to keep him in check.

==Strategy==
As with many Dark melee pushers, Gory Dark packs extreme stats and appears in swarms, but his range makes him manageable when confronted by stacks of area attackers that outrange him, such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] or [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]], as their damage will force him to repeatedly flinch before he can do much. If you have [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Weightlifter Cat]], he can kill groups of him in only a few hits, especially once his [[True Form]] and [[Wave Attack]] [[Talents|Talent]] are unlocked.

As with most Dark enemies, one [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Oda Nobunaga]] or two [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercats]] are enough to perma-[[Freeze|freeze]] this enemy and completely stop him from pushing. While he can often be pushed out of range when he does flinch, this issue is fairly negligible for the most part since any responsible DPS units won't have much trouble against him whatsoever.

